{"id": "EUVD-2026-93176", "enisaUuid": "a139d44f-c7c7-3876-9d54-87430127a073", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: percpu: Fix LSE operations on {8,16}-bit types\n\nThe assembly for __percpu_##name##_case_##sz() and\n__percpu_##name##_return_case_##sz() doesn't use the 'sfx' macro\nargument to form the LSE instruction. Without 'sfx', a W register\nargument will imply a 32-bit memory location, and consequently\n{8,16}-bit ops will erroneously read and write 32 bits of memory when\nthe LSE instruction is used.\n\nFix this by appending 'sfx' to 'op_lse' to LSE instruction. It is not\nnecessary (and not valid) to append 'sfx' to 'op_llsc', as 'op_llsc' is\na register-register operation which does not access memory (and does not\ntake a size suffix).", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d69ab4480e49bf925f4781afcc9f284affcb96b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/390742871a723b52de9b92a94c0d1c85a2531e3e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/843ace1d0a39e9b1cfcbfb3856a7b0fbdd9cd003", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8cf2093f5372952a9ebc805c418d45df7112cd14"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p97v-423w-mpcq", "CVE-2026-98248"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c2cfeab-9084-38b4-9ae2-8a7d9e247daa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "53051460-d621-385a-a227-292586149293", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "75a91473-542d-3e97-b56e-574fd8b3c420", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.0"}, {"id": "832f17e9-7348-3c82-ac97-9ec3ab08e952", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "959bf2fd03b59fc107584c21425f3dc73c49f762 <d69ab4480e49bf925f4781afcc9f284affcb96b6"}, {"id": "9cdc92f7-f906-34a7-aaae-24e247cd2b96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "959bf2fd03b59fc107584c21425f3dc73c49f762 <390742871a723b52de9b92a94c0d1c85a2531e3e"}, {"id": "afe00c95-02a6-3c5f-961c-07194f6f717b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "959bf2fd03b59fc107584c21425f3dc73c49f762 <8cf2093f5372952a9ebc805c418d45df7112cd14"}, {"id": "b1f44de0-ae19-301d-a7c3-c543a950aeca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bf10a90e-b699-3454-a857-5fe52a0fbff5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "cc0967bc-ca1f-3f9d-a628-ac3e2f0ee06f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "959bf2fd03b59fc107584c21425f3dc73c49f762 <843ace1d0a39e9b1cfcbfb3856a7b0fbdd9cd003"}, {"id": "fbaa20cd-a214-3c1b-aa6e-bb1270ba39e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0f1a5d37-e7e8-336b-8231-60cba6f9dbfd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}